(pivot_root(2) requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN/root AND that new_root be a real mount)
(point, so this is NOT auto-run in CI - deliberately no .expected file.)
(Run manually with:)
(  unshare --mount --propagation private -- \)
(    sudo ./target/release/vox tests/manual_pivot_root.vox --run)
(The unshare wraps this in a private mount namespace so it can't affect)
(your real system - pivot_root there is fully sandboxed and safe to try.)

Remove the directory called "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot/oldroot".
Remove the directory called "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot".
Create a directory called "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot".
Create a directory called "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot/oldroot".

(pivot_root requires new_root to be an actual mount point - a self)
(bind-mount is the standard trick to make an ordinary directory qualify.)
Mount "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot" at "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot" with type "none" with options "bind".
On error print "self bind-mount failed", exit 1.

Pivot root to "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot" with old root "/tmp/vox_test_pivot_newroot/oldroot".
On error print "pivot_root failed - are you root, and did the bind-mount work?", exit 1.
Print "pivot_root succeeded".

Change directory to "/".
On error print "chdir to new root failed", exit 1.
Print "chdir succeeded - process root and cwd both switched".
